    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nO'Shea O'Toole is delighted to present 17 Morley Terrace, a beautiful period home that combines original character with bright, contemporary living space. This is a well-presented and much-loved family home, finished to a high standard throughout.\n\nThe house extends to approximately 144 sq.m (1,550 sq.ft) over 3 floors. Period features begin at the front door, with its arched decorative surround and stained-glass fanlight. Inside, the elegant formal living room has a cast iron feature fireplace, a ceiling rose and original-style internal window shutters.\n\nThe heart of the home is the open-plan kitchen, dining and living area. The dining space is filled with natural light with French doors opening directly onto the rear patio. The adjoining sitting room has a solid fuel stove with a back boiler connected to the radiators, and there is a well laid out kitchen with fitted units, and open access to rear kitchen and utility area with w.c.\n\nUpstairs, 3 well appointed bedrooms and a family bathroom are on the first floor. The top floor has a generous further bedroom with its own walk-in wardrobe and w.c.\n\nThe rear garden is a real highlight. It is private and sheltered by an old stone wall and mature trees, with a paved patio and gravel areas suited to relaxing or entertaining outdoors. There is also a block-built shed, and a side entrance gives direct access to the garden from Rockfield Park.\n\nLocation\nMorley Terrace is within walking distance of Waterford City Centre. It is convenient to Plunkett Train Station, a wide choice of primary and secondary schools, SETU and local shops and services. This is a well-established and sought-after residential location, and the house will suit families, professionals and anyone looking for period charm close to the city.\n\n \n\nFeatures:\n\nBeautiful period end-of-terrace home extending to approx. 144 sq.m (1,550 sq.ft)\n\nWalking distance of Waterford City Centre\n\nBright, contemporary open-plan kitchen/dining/living area\n\nSolid fuel stove with back boiler connected to radiators\n\nTop floor bedroom with walk-in wardrobe and w.c.\n\nPrivate rear garden with block-built shed\n\nSide entrance direct to rear garden from Rockfield Park\n\nOil-fired central heating\n\nPVC double-glazed windows throughout\n\n \n\n"
      }
    ],
